This script is reading the csharp code from the given file and extracts the comments in the code where the comments start with "@@@". Then it replaces these comments with corresponding Debug.Assert statements. The replacements are based on the current implementation and previous statements.--------------------
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >= Old_arrListIndexOfX);
</code>--------------------
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX >= -1);
</code>

Here is the C# code to parse the comments which starts with "@@@" and output a corresponding Debug.Assert statement. 

```cs
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

public class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        string code = File.ReadAllText("YourFilePath.cs");
        Regex regex = new Regex("// @@@ (.*?)\\.");
        foreach (Match match in regex.Matches(code))
        {
            Console.WriteLine(string.Format("Debug.Assert({0})", match.Groups[1]));
        }
    }
}
```

You need to replace "YourFilePath.cs" with the actual path of your C# code file. This program will output a debug.assert statement for each comment starting with "@@@".--------------------
